      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a very common feeling, that hollow ache when the outside looks perfect but the inside is just... flat. Don't mistake the lack of external problems for a lack of internal substance; that gray fog is a signal that something deeper needs attention. Sometimes, the most profound quiet can be the most necessary, and that nothingness you feel is just waiting for a little nudge to become something else.",
